<title>GERMANY: RWE to complete Croatian power station.</title>
<headline>RWE to complete Croatian power station.</headline>
<dateline>ESSEN, Germany 1996-11-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>German utility RWE AG said on Sunday it will finish building of the Croatian coal-fired power station PLOMIN 2 with local utility HEP, in Croatia's first joint-venture in the electricity sector.</p>
<p>RWE said the total cost of the investment, including financing, is 350 million marks.</p>
<p>The construction of the power plant on the Istrian peninsula was interrupted in 1992. The two companies signed an agreement to complete the construction in Pula on Saturday.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
